WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx — a controlled confirmation modal (named export `ConfirmDialog`),
  mounted by destructive call sites. It composes the shared Modal + Button + Input and reproduces these branches:
    • variant danger→critical (AlertOctagon, danger token) / warning→warn (AlertTriangle, warn token) banner
      over the message (severityTokens bg/border/fg).
    • loading: both buttons inert, the confirm button shows a spinner, and backdrop-click + Escape dismissal are
      suppressed (handleModalClose / keydown both early-return while loading).
    • requireTypedConfirmation: renders an Input; confirm stays disabled until `typed === requireTypedConfirmation`
      (an empty required string is falsy → no gate). inputLabel falls back to `Type "<phrase>" to confirm`.
    • silenceKey (+ "Don't ask again" checkbox): honored ONLY when `variant !== 'danger' && !requireTypedConfirmation`.
      When the action was previously silenced the component fires onConfirm immediately and `return null` (never
      renders). On confirm it persists the silence BEFORE bubbling onConfirm (lib/confirmSilence.ts / localStorage).
  Data sources (prompt)        : `useTranslation` only — there is NO data fetch. The lone t() call is
                                 t('confirm.silence.checkbox', "Don't ask again for this action").
  Shared components (prompt)   : "(none)" listed, but the source clearly composes Modal + Button + Input — mapped to
                                 native counterparts (covenant pt 5: no parity shortcut). Documented below.
  States                       : the prompt's generic loading/empty/error/stale/offline template does NOT apply to a
                                 controlled, fetch-free presentational dialog. The source's ACTUAL branches
                                 (default danger/warning · in-flight loading · typed-confirmation gate · silence /
                                 auto-resolve) are each reproduced 1:1 (covenant pt 2: no scope narrowing, no
                                 fabricated offline/stale chips that the source does not have).

